amd, the head as it is: failed exit 0, takeover exit 0; scenarios S0=0 S1=1 S2=1 S3=1 S4=0 S5=1 S6=1 S7=1 S8=1 S9=2
E4 every later instance begins an epoch, acknowledged or not: takeover as recorded: exit 0 (the head: 0), 1 lines differ, the first: cut_numbers	PASS	the 212 cut lines are numbered 1 to 212 (state 2 counts on; state 3 counts on; state 4 counts on)
N4 a new state may begin at any number and count on from it: NOTHING differs: the recordings as recorded and every scenario give the head's lines and exits
N5 only the first line of a new state is looked at: NOTHING differs: the recordings as recorded and every scenario give the head's lines and exits
S2 the status is held to the new state's count, whichever way the state counted: S4: exit 1 (the head: 0); S5: exit 0 (the head: 1)
S3 the status's count is the cuts before the new state: failed as recorded: exit 1 (the head: 0), 1 lines differ, the first: status	FAIL	cuts '8', not '12'; S0: exit 1 (the head: 0)
F7 main judges the failure and drops the verdict: NOTHING differs: the recordings as recorded and every scenario give the head's lines and exits
A7 lost_at_kill reads the place in the whole log, not the number the line carries: NOTHING differs: the recordings as recorded and every scenario give the head's lines and exits
